cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, its data or its code, please cite the peer-reviewed article listed under preferred-citation."
title: "Replication materials for 'Regional growth, convergence, and spatial spillovers in India: A reproducible view from outer space'"
abstract: "Reproducible research compendium for a study of regional growth and convergence across 520 Indian districts between 1996 and 2010, using DMSP-OLS satellite nighttime lights as a proxy for economic activity. The repository holds the Quarto manuscript source, six computational Python notebooks, the district-level data and spatial weights matrix, the uv-locked software environment, and the rendered HTML, PDF and DOCX outputs. Every figure and table in the article is regenerated from the raw data by the notebooks."
type: software
